docs/papers204_208_sequence/scouting/finite_algebra_ninth/INTAKE.md-13-| VDF | Labelled $x\in\mathbf F_p^n$; $T_i(x)=\prod_{j\ne i}(x_i-x_j)$. Empty product at $n=1$ is $1$. | $p=2,3,5,7$, $n=1,\ldots,4$ |
docs/papers204_208_sequence/scouting/finite_algebra_ninth/INTAKE.md-14-| RHA | Positive integer compositions $x_1+\cdots+x_n=N$. Set $K=N-n$; assign $K$ units using Hamilton largest remainders with weights $1/x_i$, ties by increasing index; add one to every coordinate. | $1\le n\le4$, $n\le N\le18$ |
docs/papers204_208_sequence/scouting/finite_algebra_ninth/INTAKE.md-15-| EPN | Perfect matchings on $\{0,\ldots,2n-1\}$. Give every vertex the length of its incident old edge; sort vertices by `(length, vertex)` and pair consecutive vertices in that order. Output labels are original labels, not sorted ranks. | $n=1,\ldots,6$ |
docs/papers204_208_sequence/scouting/finite_algebra_ninth/INTAKE.md:16:| QRM | $x\in\{0,\ldots,M\}^n$. For $n\ge2$, $T_i=\lfloor\sqrt{\sum_{j\ne i}x_j^2/(n-1)}\rfloor$; $n=1$ is identity. | $1\le n\le5$, $0\le M\le4$ |
docs/papers204_208_sequence/scouting/finite_algebra_ninth/INTAKE.md-17-| QEF | $\mathbf F_p^3$; $(x,y,z)\mapsto(x+yz,y+xz,z+xy)$. Ordinary polynomial evaluation, no division or exceptional totalization. | $p=2,3,5,7,11,13$ |
